 wanted to enhance  what it feels like to take them on the  armor destruction  really enhances the battles and gives  you a more visceral experience  so the heroes can destroy all these  robotic enemies that are in the world  various parts will fall off of them they  can tear parts off of them  we turn them into physics objects and  they remain in the world for an extended  period of time so that later when you  interact with the environment all these  objects are there to react  to the the superhero moves that you make  pieces fly off enemies as you attack  them  you can see that they've been beat up  they're missing armor pieces and it  really  adds a feel of destruction to taking  down  one of those large robots  [Music]  with this type of experience we want to  make sure that we build a world that not  only  is fun to explore and learn more about  its history  but is also going to pave the way for  future storytelling experiences  this is what i love about marvel  everything has to come from story  what locations best serve the story and  what can we celebrate  there's some key places for me i mean  the helicarrier  prior to a day and being able to go  check out all the different things like  cap shield at his booth the iron man  boots seeing the hologram  we were just able to push the creative  vision further and we really invested  hard on the tech in order to make sure  that we'd be able to  support the ambition of the game we  wanted to make to enhance the  environments in marvel's avengers  we chose to add a new water simulation  that's physically based  and allows boats to float on it and  objects that get tossed in to  create a ripple effect and one of the  biggest examples of that is the  helicarrier crash  after the golden gate bridge level it  really looks like  deep ocean water and it behaves like  deep ocean water  and then going back to the helicarrier  after a day  for a lot of things like the helicarrier  that evolve over time  incrementally and i